<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yapahuwa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yapahuwa is a rock fortress in the North Western Province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a> that served as a royal capital in the late 13th century under Bhuvanaikabahu I. Its ornate stone staircase, decorated with lions, is its best-known feature. Around 1284 a Pandyan army captured the fortress and carried off the Tooth Relic of the Buddha, later recovered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parakramabahu-iii">Parakramabahu III</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yapahuwa.jpg" alt="Yapahuwa" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kurun · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yapahuwa_Lion.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
